overall-aaa-verdict: below target

The November 14 release was held when progression stopped at operation 16.
The November 21 build can be played from Live Wire through the Broadcast
Citadel shutdown, including the district consequences, epilogue and ranking.

## Release verification

All 666 repository tests passed in 31 suites, including 159 Signalbreak tests.
In a fresh localhost Edge campaign, player controls and live AI produced 20
consecutive victories with all four engineers extracted on every operation.
The local leaderboard received a rank GET and score POST for 72,820 points.
A supported clean shutdown on a phone viewport raised the saved best to 73,420.

All 120 operation/viewport checks passed at 320×568, 390×844, 844×390,
768×1024, 1440×900 and 3840×2160. Keyboard and emulated touch orders, reload,
offline file boot and DPR2 passed. The sweep found no browser errors or
horizontal overflow. Reviewed the opening and finale briefings and boards at
all six sizes, every 320px board, and both earned epilogues. Larger views
were reduced on the review sheets. All eight runtime hashes matched the
browser manifest in node_modules/.cache/signalbreak/release-2026-11-21.

## Final recorded critic verdicts

- Environment and character art. XCOM 2 won overall. The latest art reviewer
  passed identification of both rooftop stairs and lift occupancy. Riders
  still cluster at 320px, and several districts lack recognizable landmarks.
- Tactical rules and feedback. The latest rules reviewer passed the exposed
  ward, threatened engineer and medal feedback. Earlier reviewers passed the
  timed breaker warning and rear-pursuer markers. XCOM 2 remained easier to
  read for cover and character roles at normal phone zoom.
- Campaign presentation and interface. The finale reviewers found the two
  sources of district support and their effects readable after revision.
  XCOM 2 won the overall comparison. The epilogue relies on text over a
  tactical map. Short screens require scrolling and wide maps leave unused space.
- Audio and animated VFX have no independent passing verdict. Human play,
  physical-device touch, listening and real-device performance remain unverified.

Operations 09–18 describe their optional mastery objectives but still lack
persisted medals. Operations 01–08 and 19–20 track awards. The public build
retains its FIRST PLAYABLE / FULL CAMPAIGN IN DEVELOPMENT label.
